{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion","title":"thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":810,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:submersion-inner-congr]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:local-section-manifold]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-submersion]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth]]","[[#REF:ch2-6]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion-inner]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion","line":1274,"source":"\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion}\n\n\\uses{prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique, lem:submersion-inner-congr, prop:local-section-manifold, def:riemannian-submersion, lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth, lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth, REF:ch2-6}\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.28}\n\n\n\nLet $(\\tilde M,\\tilde g)$ be Riemannian, let $\\pi:\\tilde M\\to M$ be a surjective smooth submersion, and let $G$ act on $\\tilde M$. If the action is isometric, vertical, and transitive on fibers, then a unique Riemannian metric on $M$ makes $\\pi$ a Riemannian submersion.\n\\end{theorem}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique,lem:submersion-inner-congr,prop:local-section-manifold,def:submersion-inner,def:riemannian-submersion,lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth,lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth}\n\\sketch Define $g_y=\\beta_x$ for any $x$ with $\\pi(x)=y$; this is well defined by Lemma \\ref{lem:submersion-inner-congr}, symmetric, and positive definite because $L_xu\\ne0$ for $u\\ne0$. A local section $\\sigma$ of $\\pi$ gives $g_y(u,v)=\\tilde g_{\\sigma(y)}(L_{\\sigma(y)}u,L_{\\sigma(y)}v)$. Lemma \\ref{lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth} and Lemma \\ref{lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth} make this smooth. Finally the defining identity holds on horizontal vectors since $L_xd\\pi_x$ is the identity on $H_x$. Uniqueness is Proposition \\ref{prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section> <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a67726f75702d616374696f6e2d7269656d616e6e69616e2d7375626d657273696f6e\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ariemannian-submersion-metric-unique\">↗ prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Asubmersion-inner-congr\">↗ lem:submersion-inner-congr</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixA%23prop%3Alocal-section-manifold\">↗ prop:local-section-manifold</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-submersion\">↗ def:riemannian-submersion</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Abilinear-comp-of-family-smooth\">↗ lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth\">↗ lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth</a> <span class=\"unresolved tex-use\">↗ REF:ch2-6</span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.28</span></span><p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(\\tilde M,\\tilde g)$\">$(\\tilde M,\\tilde g)$</span> be Riemannian, let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi :\\tilde M\\to M$\">$\\pi :\\tilde M\\to M$</span> be a surjective smooth submersion, and let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$G$\">$G$</span> act on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde M$\">$\\tilde M$</span>. If the action is isometric, vertical, and transitive on fibers, then a unique Riemannian metric on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> makes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi $\">$\\pi $</span> a Riemannian submersion.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ariemannian-submersion-metric-unique\">↗ prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Asubmersion-inner-congr\">↗ lem:submersion-inner-congr</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixA%23prop%3Alocal-section-manifold\">↗ prop:local-section-manifold</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asubmersion-inner\">↗ def:submersion-inner</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-submersion\">↗ def:riemannian-submersion</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Abilinear-comp-of-family-smooth\">↗ lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth\">↗ lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth</a> \\sketch Define <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g_y=\\beta _x$\">$g_y=\\beta _x$</span> for any <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi (x)=y$\">$\\pi (x)=y$</span>; this is well defined by Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Asubmersion-inner-congr\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:submersion-inner-congr\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7375626d657273696f6e2d696e6e65722d636f6e6772\">3</a>, symmetric, and positive definite because <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$L_xu\\ne 0$\">$L_xu\\ne 0$</span> for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u\\ne 0$\">$u\\ne 0$</span>. A local section <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sigma $\">$\\sigma $</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi $\">$\\pi $</span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g_y(u,v)=\\tilde g_{\\sigma (y)}(L_{\\sigma (y)}u,L_{\\sigma (y)}v)$\">$g_y(u,v)=\\tilde g_{\\sigma (y)}(L_{\\sigma (y)}u,L_{\\sigma (y)}v)$</span>. Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a686f72697a6f6e74616c2d6c6966742d696e2d636f6f7264696e617465732d736d6f6f7468\">3</a> and Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Abilinear-comp-of-family-smooth\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a62696c696e6561722d636f6d702d6f662d66616d696c792d736d6f6f7468\">17</a> make this smooth. Finally the defining identity holds on horizontal vectors since <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$L_xd\\pi _x$\">$L_xd\\pi _x$</span> is the identity on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$H_x$\">$H_x$</span>. Uniqueness is Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ariemannian-submersion-metric-unique\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a7269656d616e6e69616e2d7375626d657273696f6e2d6d65747269632d756e69717565\">3</a>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["Blueprint 依赖不存在或不唯一: REF:ch2-6","部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#cor:quotient-manifold-lie-group-riemannian-metric","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique","title":"prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique","label":"prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:submersion-inner-congr","title":"lem:submersion-inner-congr","label":"lem:submersion-inner-congr"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:local-section-manifold","title":"prop:local-section-manifold","label":"prop:local-section-manifold"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-submersion","title":"def:riemannian-submersion","label":"def:riemannian-submersion"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth","title":"lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth","label":"lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth","title":"lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth","label":"lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion-inner","title":"def:submersion-inner","label":"def:submersion-inner"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#cor:quotient-manifold-lie-group-riemannian-metric","title":"cor:quotient-manifold-lie-group-riemannian-metric","label":"cor:quotient-manifold-lie-group-riemannian-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:fubini-study-metric","title":"ex:fubini-study-metric","label":"ex:fubini-study-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-covering-metric","title":"prop:riemannian-covering-metric","label":"prop:riemannian-covering-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prob:riemannian-metric-submersion","title":"prob:riemannian-metric-submersion","label":"prob:riemannian-metric-submersion"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion","title":"thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion","tex":"\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion}\n\n\\uses{prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique, lem:submersion-inner-congr, prop:local-section-manifold, def:riemannian-submersion, lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth, lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth, REF:ch2-6}\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.28}\n\n\n\nLet $(\\tilde M,\\tilde g)$ be Riemannian, let $\\pi:\\tilde M\\to M$ be a surjective smooth submersion, and let $G$ act on $\\tilde M$. If the action is isometric, vertical, and transitive on fibers, then a unique Riemannian metric on $M$ makes $\\pi$ a Riemannian submersion.\n\\end{theorem}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique,lem:submersion-inner-congr,prop:local-section-manifold,def:submersion-inner,def:riemannian-submersion,lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth,lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth}\n\\sketch Define $g_y=\\beta_x$ for any $x$ with $\\pi(x)=y$; this is well defined by Lemma \\ref{lem:submersion-inner-congr}, symmetric, and positive definite because $L_xu\\ne0$ for $u\\ne0$. A local section $\\sigma$ of $\\pi$ gives $g_y(u,v)=\\tilde g_{\\sigma(y)}(L_{\\sigma(y)}u,L_{\\sigma(y)}v)$. Lemma \\ref{lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth} and Lemma \\ref{lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth} make this smooth. Finally the defining identity holds on horizontal vectors since $L_xd\\pi_x$ is the identity on $H_x$. Uniqueness is Proposition \\ref{prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique}.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique","title":"prop:riemannian-submersion-metric-unique","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:submersion-inner-congr","title":"lem:submersion-inner-congr","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:local-section-manifold","title":"prop:local-section-manifold","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-submersion","title":"def:riemannian-submersion","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth","title":"lem:bilinear-comp-of-family-smooth","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth","title":"lem:horizontal-lift-in-coordinates-smooth","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion-inner","title":"def:submersion-inner","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":["[[#REF:ch2-6]]","REF:ch2-6"],"unresolved_omitted":0}}